<h2>Questions from Dover property owners</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>I’m being reassigned from Dover AFB during my claim. Can you still help?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Yes. We can inspect with your permission and a local contact, and handle the rest remotely.</p></div></details><details><summary>Does my historic district home need special pricing?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Often. Historic materials and any design-review requirements can increase repair costs, and we document them so they’re not treated as upgrades.</p></div></details><details><summary>Are tornado claims common in Kent County?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Less common than wind and hail claims, but they happen, usually with summer storms or tropical remnants.</p></div></details></div>
